{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1488313-tc-adventure-travel-times-in-1920-30s","id":1488313,"title":"[TC Adventure!] Travel times in 1920-30s","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-28T20:53:43-07:00","id":1488313,"title":"[TC Adventure!] Travel times in 1920-30s","content":"A bit handy topic. <b>How fast people fly, sail and move in 1920-30s?</b><br /> <br /> I prepare <b>Adventure!</b> story with travel from London to India and back in 1923. <b>What would be optimal means of transport for PCs then?</b><br /> <br /> From what I read, <a href=\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/wales/entries/09bb8d10-07b8-3066-ba93-22b7b795cf4b\" target=\"_blank\">first direct flights from London to India started from 1929</a>. Before that flew plains on few transfers in between?<br /> <br /> <b>How long would take to sail from London to India in 1920s? </b>Two weeks, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T21:38:35-07:00","id":1488318,"title":"","content":"There are 2 main issues for flight durng the 20s-30s, first is the flight speed that is about 100-200 km/h (today plane fly at 800-1000 km/h), and second is the autonomy, how far does a plane go before needing to refil the fuel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T00:52:57-07:00","id":1488334,"title":"","content":"From what I'm seeing on Google Maps, from London to Kolkata is circa 1300 km. So it would be like 12-15 hours non-stop flight at 100km/h - but you need, probably, take about 3-4 stops to refill and recharge of the pilot, maybe switching between two co-pilots. <b>So flying till Kolkata should take day, maybe day and half? </b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T01:19:26-07:00","id":1488337,"title":"","content":"Or more... better than the week or so that it would take by boat, or the months by car.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T01:41:40-07:00","id":1488338,"title":"","content":"Achievement flight in from UK to India in 1929 took 50 hours - so before it - it would take at least twice the time, with all the transfers and refuelings.<br /> <br /> <i>'<span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:ReithSans\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The two men in question were Squadron Leader Arthur Jones-Williams and his co-pilot Flight Lieutenant Norman Jenkins. Flying a Fairey Long-Range Monoplane \u2013 one of two built specifically for the RAF Long Range Development Unit - they set off from the RAF base at Cranwell on 24 April 1929. 50 hours (and 38 minutes) later they arrived at Karachi in the sub-continent.' </span></span></span></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T02:09:15-07:00","id":1488341,"title":"","content":"See if you can find some <b>Call of Cthulhu </b> materials. Their Players Handbook equivalents had good materials on travel times and conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T12:47:56-07:00","id":1488481,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Call of Cthulhu 7th <i>Investigators Handbook </i>- Travel Speeds for 1920s</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Average Aircraft Speeds and Ranges, circa 1928:</b><br /> Single-engine \u00ad xed-wing aircraft, 120 mph (190 kph), 300-500 miles (480-800 km).<br /> S Twin-engine \u00ad xed-wing aircraft, 90 mph (144 kph), 500-800 miles (800-1280 km).<br /> S Zeppelin, 70 mph (112 kph), 1000 miles (1600 km).<br /> <b>Average Ship Speeds, 1920: </b><br /> S Motorboat, 22 knots (25 mph, 40 kph).<br /> S Freighter, 14 knots (16 mph, 25 kph).<br /> S Atlantic Liner, 25 knots (29 mph, 46 kph).<br /> <b>Average Speed on Horseback: </b><br /> S 12 mph (18 kph).<br /> <b>Average Carriage Speed: </b><br /> S 10 mph (16 kph).<br /> <b>Average Auto Speed, 1920s: </b><br /> S 25 mph (40 kph); back roads 15 mph (24 kph).<br /> <b>Average Long Distance Rail Speed: </b><br /> S 35 mph (55 kph). In the United States, this rate has not much changed in a century<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T13:31:42-07:00","id":1488486,"title":"","content":"One thing that I would like to point out is that there's a high chance that player characters could have access to technological superior transportation methods. Let's say then that they can use vehicles that are 10 to 20 years more advanced that what is available, how much would travel times change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T15:44:06-07:00","id":1488500,"title":"","content":"I would say most vehicles in the 20-30s would have a maximum speed scale 3, and super tech can go above it. You may have a rocket and land in the moon, like Tintin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T18:14:30-07:00","id":1488514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1488313-tc-adventure-travel-times-in-1920-30s?p=1488486#post1488486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that I would like to point out is that there's a high chance that player characters could have access to technological superior transportation methods. Let's say then that they can use vehicles that are 10 to 20 years more advanced that what is available, how much would travel times change?</div> </div> </div> </div>Roads were more of an issue than cars. Modern cars wouldn't go much faster on 1920's roads. Off road vehicles until the 1960s would only achieve about the same speed as normal cars just off of any kind of road. And it would be a brutally bumpy ride. A 1950s off road vehicle on ordinary 1920s roads would be about 10 mph faster than contemporary cars. Something like a Duesenberg might go faster. But at higher maintenance and fuel costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T06:34:32-07:00","id":1488560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1488313-tc-adventure-travel-times-in-1920-30s?p=1488514#post1488514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Roads were more of an issue than cars. Modern cars wouldn't go much faster on 1920's roads. Off road vehicles until the 1960s would only achieve about the same speed as normal cars just off of any kind of road. And it would be a brutally bumpy ride. A 1950s off road vehicle on ordinary 1920s roads would be about 10 mph faster than contemporary cars. Something like a Duesenberg might go faster. But at higher maintenance and fuel costs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What about boats and planes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T08:08:23-07:00","id":1488566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1488313-tc-adventure-travel-times-in-1920-30s?p=1488560#post1488560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What about boats and planes?</div> </div> </div> </div>With boats the typical navigational hazards still apply. Besides, because the USA more or less guaranteed the freedom of the seas from the late forties until fairly recently, most ships actually go slower than they did in the twenties for economic reasons.<br /> <br /> Planes also face navigation issues but there you'd get the full benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T09:36:19-07:00","id":1488571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1488313-tc-adventure-travel-times-in-1920-30s?p=1488566#post1488566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With boats the typical navigational hazards still apply. Besides, because the USA more or less guaranteed the freedom of the seas from the late forties until fairly recently, most ships actually go slower than they did in the twenties for economic reasons.<br /> <br /> Planes also face navigation issues but there you'd get the full benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your answers. I didn't really think about the importance of infrastructure for land vehicles. That said, even if boats, planes and cars are not much faster, could they have other advantages? More comfortable, better radio equipment, less fuel consumption, etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T01:12:46-07:00","id":1488676,"title":"","content":"Remembering car trips in the 1960s (I'll be 62 in October) yes! Today's cars are more comfortable. Remember &quot;car sickness&quot; used to be a common trope, like jokes about the milk man, both have faded from common memory. It's like my trying to tell an exchange student from Colombia that boarding houses were commonplace in the USA until the 1940s. ( I wasn't believed). <br /> <br /> One note on how much more comfortable today's cars are. Howard Johnson's used to be a major restaurant chain. Their food, until the 1970s, was plain but very high quality. Exactly what people on road trips wanted after a day of constant vibration and auto fumes. Food that wasn't plain would have been nauseating. With just the improvements of the early 1970s road trips became more comfortable and spicier food more desirable. (Also Howard Johnson's changed management, which meant the food went from plain but good to plain and dull, which killed the chain).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T09:27:11-08:00","id":1500375,"title":"","content":"An Advanced version or modified version of the Douglas DC-3 would likely be common <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douglas_DC-3\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/df/Douglas_DC-3%2C_SE-CFP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douglas_DC-3\" target=\"_blank\"> Douglas DC-3 - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douglas_DC-3\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douglas_DC-3 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T10:11:18-08:00","id":1500377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheWanderingJewels</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1488313-tc-adventure-travel-times-in-1920-30s?p=1500375#post1500375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Advanced version or modified version of the Douglas DC-3 would likely be common <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douglas_DC-3\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douglas_DC-3</a></div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. But almost no one flew at night if they could help it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}